        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kuku",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "kuku"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " gets its deep green colour from the quantity of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "sabzi",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sabzi"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " used: roughly 250g of herbs to 6 eggs. The herbs are not a garnish here. They are the main ingredient. The barberries and walnuts add bursts of tartness and crunch. Serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The kuku is cooked on the hob rather than in the oven. You flip it halfway through cooking to brown both sides. It can also be finished under a grill to avoid the flip."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
